{
  "slug": "clay",
  "name": "Clay",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Work with Clay from Claude Code: set up and sign in to the clay CLI, query and analyze Clay tables, search Clay's GTM database for people and companies, manage audiences, signals, routines and workflows, and draft and review Sequencer campaigns. Includes hooks that auto-approve the plugin's own clay CLI calls and Clay skills; requires a Clay account.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **31 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (31): `audiences` (Clay Audiences — the workspace's own people, companies, and deals (contacts, leads, accounts, customers)), `campaigns` (Inspect, create, compare, analyze, and edit Clay Campaigns or Sequencer campaigns through the clay CLI), `campaigns-interview` (Use when a fresh Clay Sequencer campaign has no meaningful subject or body copy and needs its first…), `campaigns-sequence-reviewing` (Review Clay Sequencer copy as the intended recipient and identify only material, actionable objections), `campaigns-sequence-writing` (Draft and revise complete Clay Sequencer email sequences using supplied campaign strategy and context), `clay` (Clay — start here), `clay-feedback` (Clay feedback — send a bug report or product feedback to the Clay team via the `clay feedback`…), `cli` (Clay CLI — the primary scripting surface (JSON output, typed errors)), and 23 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install clay@claude-plugins-official` from `clay-run/agent-plugins` (`clay`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
